<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal details 1998/99 privatisation plan.</title>
<headline>Portugal details 1998/99 privatisation plan.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the list of companies that the Portuguese government plans to privatise or further privatise in 1998-99.</p>
<p>    Company					   Intended sale date</p>
<p>    ANA-Aeroportos &amp; Navegacao Aerea, EP		    98..</p>
<p>    BRISA-Autoestradas de Portugal, SA (phase 2)	  99..</p>
<p>    CIMPOR-Cimentos de Portugal (phase 3)		   98..</p>
<p>    CL-Companhia das Lezirias, SA			     98..</p>
<p>    DRAGAPOR-Dragagens de Portugal, SA			98..</p>
<p>    EDP-Electricidade de Portugal, SA (phse 2)	    99..</p>
<p>    ENVC-Estaleiros Navais de Viana do Castelo, SA     98/99..</p>
<p>    EPAC - Empresa Para Agroalimentacao e Cereais, SA  98/99..</p>
<p>    GDP-Gas de Portugal (SGPS) SA			    98/99..</p>
<p>    PEC-Produtos Pecuarios SGPS				98/99..</p>
<p>    Petrogal-Petroleos de Portugal, SA (final phase)    98..</p>
<p>    Portucel-Emp.Celulose Papel de Portugal, SGPS, SA   98..</p>
<p>    SILOPOR- Empresa de Silos Portuarios, SA		98..</p>
<p>    SN-Empresa de Servicos, SA				  98..</p>
<p>    TABAQUEIRA-Empresa Ind. de Tabacos, SA (phases 2&amp;3) 99..</p>
<p>    TAP-Transportadora Aerea Portuguesa, SA		98/99..</p>
<p>    Tertir-Terminais de Portugal, SA			  98..</p>
<p>-- Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
